{"format":1,"key":"zone:redridge","path":"/lore/zone/redridge","name":"Redridge Mountains","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"redridge","name":"Redridge Mountains","path":"/lore/zone/redridge"},"levels":"Levels 15-25","description":"East of Elwynn Forest, the Redridge Mountains feature rushing rivers, wooded slopes, and the serene expanse of Lake Everstill. Despite its scenic…","intro":["East of Elwynn Forest, the Redridge Mountains feature rushing rivers, wooded slopes, and the serene expanse of Lake Everstill. Despite its scenic heights, the region is besieged by hostile Shadowhide gnolls and the encroaching Blackrock orcs of the Dark Horde. With the kingdom's military tied up by internal strife in Stormwind, the lakeside town of Lakeshire must rely on wandering mercenaries to hold the line."],"sections":[{"t":"A Bastion Under Siege","p":["The Redridge range was once among the most peaceful corners of the kingdom, supplying Stormwind with timber, freshwater fish, and crops. Today, that quiet life has eroded. The lakeside township of Lakeshire sits perpetually fortified against aggressive incursions. To the east, Stonewatch Keep—once a proud bastion of the kingdom—has fallen under the control of renegade Blackrock orcs, cutting off roads and threatening to overrun the eastern valleys entirely."]},{"t":"The Divided Range","p":["Geographically, these peaks form part of the spine running down the subcontinent of Azeroth. Centuries ago, the mountain chain reached much farther north until the Dark Iron clan inadvertently summoned the Firelord Ragnaros, tearing the earth asunder and creating the fiery crater of Blackrock Mountain. That cataclysm severed the northern peaks into the ash-choked Burning Steppes, leaving only the southern Redridge valleys lush, green, and vulnerable to attacks descending from the slopes above."]},{"t":"Neglected by the Crown","p":["While Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris plead for reinforcements, the regency council in Stormwind has effectively abandoned Lakeshire to fend for itself. Desperate entreaties sent to Sentinel Hill and Darkshire yield nothing, as both sister settlements are crippled by their own crises. With reinforcements nowhere in sight, local magistrates must hire any capable sellsword willing to brave the Lakeridge Highway, clear the gnoll camps, and push back the shadow looming over Lake Everstill."]}],"clips":[],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Redridge Mountains (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Redridge_Mountains_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Redridge Mountains","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Redridge_Mountains"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakeshire","n":"Lakeshire","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lake-everstill","n":"Lake Everstill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/stonewatch-keep","n":"Stonewatch Keep","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/magistrate-solomon","n":"Magistrate Solomon","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/marshal-marris","n":"Marshal Marris","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/zone/burningsteppes","n":"Burning Steppes","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/elwynn","n":"Elwynn Forest","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/duskwood","n":"Duskwood","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/eastvale-logging-camp","n":"Eastvale Logging Camp","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/jerod-s-landing","n":"Jerod's Landing","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ridgepoint-tower","n":"Ridgepoint Tower","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/tower-of-azora","n":"Tower of Azora","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/alther-s-mill","n":"Alther's Mill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/galardell-valley","n":"Galardell Valley","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lake-everstill","n":"Lake Everstill","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakeridge-highway","n":"Lakeridge Highway","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakeshire","n":"Lakeshire","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakeshire-inn","n":"Lakeshire Inn","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lakeshire-town-hall","n":"Lakeshire Town Hall","k":"s